I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to pull live weather data or make external API calls. However, I can point you toward a few reliable ways to get the hourly forecast for the coordinates you provided (37.8651 N, 119.5383 W – roughly the center of Yosemite National Park) for the next 10 days:

| Service | How to use | What you’ll get |
|---------|------------|-----------------|
| **OpenWeatherMap** | 1. Sign up for a free account at https://openweathermap.org/. <br>2. Get an API key. <br>3. Call the “One Call API” endpoint: <br>   `https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/onecall?lat=37.8651&lon=-119.5383&exclude=current,minutely,daily,alerts&units=imperial&appid=YOUR_KEY` <br>4. The response contains an `hourly` array with temperature (`temp`), wind speed (`wind_speed`), and precipitation (`rain`/`snow`). | Hourly data for up to 48 h; you can combine multiple calls or use the “forecast” endpoint for 7‑day forecasts. |
| **WeatherAPI.com** | 1. Register at https://www.weatherapi.com/. <br>2. Use the “Forecast” endpoint: <br>   `https://api.weatherapi.com/v1/forecast.json?key=YOUR_KEY&q=37.8651,-119.5383&days=10&aqi=no&alerts=no` <br>3. Parse the `forecast.forecastday[].hour[]` array. | Full 10‑day forecast with hourly details (temp_c, wind_kph, precip_mm, etc.). |
| **NOAA Climate Data Online (CDO)** | 1. Find the nearest NOAA station (e.g., “USC00100001” – Fresno Airport). <br>2. Use the CDO API: <br>   `https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/cdo-web/api/v2/data?datasetid=GHCND&stationid=USC00100001&startdate=2024-10-20&enddate=2024-10-30&datatypeid=TMIN,TMAX,WINDSPD,PRCP&limit=1000` <br>3. You’ll need a token from https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/cdo-web/token. | Daily summaries; not hourly, but useful for long‑term trends. |
| **AccuWeather** | 1. Create an account at https://developer.accuweather.com/. <br>2. Use the “Hourly Forecast” endpoint: <br>   `https://dataservice.accuweather.com/forecasts/v1/hourly/10day?apikey=YOUR_KEY&q=37.8651,-119.5383&metric=true` | 10‑day hourly forecast (temp, wind, precipitation). |

### Quick example with WeatherAPI (JSON)

```json
{
  "location": {
    "name": "Yosemite",
    "lat": 37.8651,
    "lon": -119.5383
  },
  "forecast": {
    "forecastday": [
      {
        "date": "2024-10-20",
        "hour": [
          {
            "time": "00:00",
            "temp_c": 12.3,
            "wind_kph": 15.2,
            "precip_mm": 0.0
          },
          {
            "time": "01:00",
            "temp_c": 11.8,
            "wind_kph": 14.8,
            "precip_mm": 0.0
          },
          ...
        ]
      },
      ...
    ]
  }
}
```

### Tips for handling the data

1. **Units** – Most APIs let you choose metric or imperial. Pick what’s most convenient for you.
2. **Time zone** – The API will return times in UTC or local time depending on the endpoint. Convert to your local time zone if needed.
3. **Precipitation** – Some APIs return separate rain and snow fields; you may want to sum them for total precipitation.
4. **Rate limits** – Free tiers often limit requests per minute/day. Cache results if you’re building an app.

If you’d like, I can help you write a small script (Python, JavaScript, etc.) that pulls this data once you have an API key. Just let me know which service you prefer!
